# Tests for the Hoh_qss_persons module

Run with `clerk test`. Each named scope is one concrete person (or household),
worked by hand from IRC 2(a), 2(b), 7703(b) and Pub. 501 (2024) pp 9-11 as
quoted in `catala/hoh_qss_persons.catala_en`. Every scope sets satisfiable
inputs (answers a real filer could give) and asserts the expected result and
the rejection of the wrong one. The oracle comparison is
`make difftest-persons` (per-person Direct File values, `oracle/persons.csv`).

> Using Types
> Using Qualifying_child as Q
> Using Qualifying_relative as R
> Using Dependents_benefit_split as B
> Using Hoh_qss_persons as H

## Helper: one household member and the filer, with default answers

The default person is the filer's biological son, born 2016-05-01 (8),
unmarried, a U.S. citizen with an SSN, who lived with the filer all year, had
no gross income, did not provide over half of his own support, is nobody
else's qualifying child, and is claimed. The filer (born 1985-06-15) is
unmarried (`eligible_for_mfj` false), could qualify for HoH but not QSS,
cannot be claimed by anyone, paid more than half the cost of keeping up the
home, and did not pay for a parent's separate home. No benefit split. A test
overrides only what it tests; `r` is the person's result.

```catala
declaration scope Case:
  context relationship content Q.Relationship
  context date_of_birth content date
  context residency content Q.ResidencyDuration
  context married content boolean
  context writable_joint_return content boolean
  context own_support content boolean
  context could_be_qc_of_another content boolean
  context potential_claimer_must_file content boolean
  context gross_income content money
  context qr_support content boolean
  context tin_type content R.TinType
  context citizen content boolean
  context tp_claims content boolean
  # The filer is the custodial parent who signed Form 8332 (IRC 152(e)(2))
  context custodial_release content boolean
  # The filer is a grandparent who reached the non-parent split with a lower
  # AGI than the parent (Pub 501 p 18, Example 2)
  context grandparent_lower_agi content boolean
  context upkeep content boolean
  context parent_upkeep content boolean
  context eligible_for_mfj content boolean
  context filer_could_qualify_for_hoh content boolean
  context filer_could_qualify_for_qss content boolean
  context minimum_filer_date_of_birth content date
  output member content H.Member
  output r content H.HohQssPersonTest

scope Case:
  definition relationship equals Q.Relationship.BiologicalChild
  definition date_of_birth equals |2016-05-01|
  definition residency equals Q.ResidencyDuration.AllYear
  definition married equals false
  definition writable_joint_return equals false
  definition own_support equals false
  definition could_be_qc_of_another equals false
  definition potential_claimer_must_file equals false
  definition gross_income equals $0
  definition qr_support equals true
  definition tin_type equals R.TinType.Ssn
  definition citizen equals true
  definition tp_claims equals true
  definition custodial_release equals false
  definition grandparent_lower_agi equals false
  definition upkeep equals true
  definition parent_upkeep equals false
  definition eligible_for_mfj equals false
  definition filer_could_qualify_for_hoh equals true
  definition filer_could_qualify_for_qss equals false
  definition minimum_filer_date_of_birth equals |1985-06-15|
  definition member equals H.Member {
    -- dependent: R.Member {
      -- person: Q.Person {
           -- relationship: relationship
           -- date_of_birth: date_of_birth
           -- full_time_student: false
           -- permanent_total_disability: false
           -- residency_duration: residency
           -- own_support: own_support
           -- married: married
           -- writable_joint_return: writable_joint_return
           -- writable_required_to_file: writable_joint_return
           -- writable_filing_only_for_refund: false
           -- writable_could_be_qualifying_child_of_another: could_be_qc_of_another
           -- writable_potential_claimer_must_file: potential_claimer_must_file
           -- writable_potential_claimer_did_file: potential_claimer_must_file
           -- writable_potential_claimer_filed_only_for_refund: false }
      -- answers: R.DependentAnswers {
           -- gross_income: gross_income
           -- writable_qr_support_test: qr_support
           -- tin_type: tin_type
           -- is_us_citizen_full_year: citizen
           -- writable_us_resident: false
           -- writable_us_national: false
           -- writable_canada_mexico_resident: false
           -- tp_claims: tp_claims }
      -- split: B.BenefitSplitAnswers {
           -- has_other_biological_or_adoptive_parent: custodial_release
           -- non_parental_some_parent_not_claiming: grandparent_lower_agi
           -- which_parent_not_claiming:
                if custodial_release then B.WrittenDeclaration.IDid
                else B.WrittenDeclaration.NobodyDid
           -- in_parents_custody: custodial_release or grandparent_lower_agi
           -- lived_with_tp_or_other_biological_or_adoptive_parent_more_than_six_months:
                custodial_release
           -- biological_or_adoptive_parents_living: grandparent_lower_agi
           -- nights_with_tp_vs_other_parent:
                if custodial_release then B.NightsComparison.More
                else B.NightsComparison.Less
           -- tp_agi_higher_than_other_parent: false
           -- parents_meet_reqs_rule_for_children_of_divorced_parents:
                grandparent_lower_agi
           -- special_rule_child_used_by_custodial_parent_as_qp: false
           -- special_rule_agi_test: false
           -- parental_situation:
                if custodial_release then B.ParentalSituation.DivorcedOrSeparated
                else B.ParentalSituation.Other
           -- parental_support: custodial_release
           -- multiple_support_agreement: false } }
    -- upkeep: H.UpkeepAnswers {
         -- tp_paid_most_of_home_upkeep: upkeep
         -- tp_paid_most_of_parent_home_upkeep: parent_upkeep } }
  definition r equals
    output of H.HohQssPersonTest with {
      -- member: member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: minimum_filer_date_of_birth
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true
      -- treat_as_mfj: false
      -- eligible_for_mfj: eligible_for_mfj
      -- filer_could_qualify_for_hoh: filer_could_qualify_for_hoh
      -- filer_could_qualify_for_qss: filer_could_qualify_for_qss }
```

## The cases of issue #19

### Child path: a qualifying child, the filer paid most of the upkeep

IRC 2(b)(1)(A)(i); Pub. 501 p 9, Example 1 (an unmarried child who is your
qualifying child). Known-bad output rejected: the same child without the
upkeep is not a qualifying person (2(b)(1), "over half of the cost of
maintaining the household").

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestChildPath:
  c scope Case
  no_upkeep scope Case

scope TestChildPath:
  definition no_upkeep.upkeep equals false
  assertion c.r.dep.qualifying_child
  assertion c.r.hoh_qualifying_child_path
  assertion not c.r.hoh_parent_path and not c.r.hoh_other_relative_path
  assertion c.r.hoh_qualifying_person
  assertion c.r.person_qualifies_tp_for_hoh
  # Known-bad: no upkeep, no qualifying person
  assertion no_upkeep.r.dep.qualifying_child
  assertion not no_upkeep.r.hoh_qualifying_child_path
  assertion not no_upkeep.r.hoh_qualifying_person
```

### Parent path: a dependent parent living apart, the filer pays for the parent's home

IRC 2(b)(1)(B); Pub. 501 p 9, Special rule for parent. The filer's mother,
74, lives in her own apartment (less than six months with the filer), had
$3,000 of gross income, and the filer paid over half her support and over
half the cost of her apartment. Known-bad outputs rejected: the same mother
with $5,050 of gross income cannot be claimed (IRC 152(d)(1)(B)), so she is
not a qualifying person (Table 4 row 2); and paying for the filer's own home
instead of the parent's home does not count.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestParentPath:
  c scope Case
  high_income scope Case
  own_home_only scope Case

scope TestParentPath:
  definition c.relationship equals Q.Relationship.Parent
  definition c.date_of_birth equals |1950-04-02|
  definition c.residency equals Q.ResidencyDuration.LessThanSixMonths
  definition c.gross_income equals $3,000
  definition c.upkeep equals false
  definition c.parent_upkeep equals true
  definition high_income.relationship equals Q.Relationship.Parent
  definition high_income.date_of_birth equals |1950-04-02|
  definition high_income.residency equals Q.ResidencyDuration.LessThanSixMonths
  definition high_income.gross_income equals $5,050
  definition high_income.upkeep equals false
  definition high_income.parent_upkeep equals true
  definition own_home_only.relationship equals Q.Relationship.Parent
  definition own_home_only.date_of_birth equals |1950-04-02|
  definition own_home_only.residency equals Q.ResidencyDuration.LessThanSixMonths
  definition own_home_only.gross_income equals $3,000
  definition own_home_only.upkeep equals true
  definition own_home_only.parent_upkeep equals false
  assertion c.r.is_parent
  assertion c.r.dep.qualifying_relative and c.r.dep.eligible_dependent
  assertion c.r.flow_add_person_keeping_up_parents_home
  assertion c.r.hoh_parent_path
  assertion c.r.hoh_qualifying_person
  assertion not c.r.hoh_other_relative_path
  # Known-bad: not a dependent
  assertion not high_income.r.dep.eligible_dependent
  assertion not high_income.r.hoh_qualifying_person
  # Known-bad: the filer's own home does not house the parent
  assertion not own_home_only.r.hoh_parent_path
  assertion not own_home_only.r.hoh_other_relative_path
  assertion not own_home_only.r.hoh_qualifying_person
```

### Other-relative path: a brother who lived with the filer more than half the year

IRC 2(b)(1)(A)(ii); Pub. 501 p 10, Table 4 row 3. The filer's brother, 34 (so
not a qualifying child), lived with the filer eight months, had $2,000 of
gross income and was supported over half by the filer. Known-bad outputs
rejected: the same brother living with the filer less than six months
("your relative didn't live with you more than half the year: not a
qualifying person"), and a friend who lived with the filer all year (Pub. 501
p 9, Example 3: a qualifying relative only under 152(d)(2)(H), excluded by
IRC 2(b)(3)(B)(i)).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestOtherRelativePath:
  c scope Case
  short scope Case
  friend scope Case

scope TestOtherRelativePath:
  definition c.relationship equals Q.Relationship.Sibling
  definition c.date_of_birth equals |1990-01-01|
  definition c.residency equals Q.ResidencyDuration.SixToElevenMonths
  definition c.gross_income equals $2,000
  definition short.relationship equals Q.Relationship.Sibling
  definition short.date_of_birth equals |1990-01-01|
  definition short.residency equals Q.ResidencyDuration.LessThanSixMonths
  definition short.gross_income equals $2,000
  definition friend.relationship equals Q.Relationship.NoneOfTheAbove
  definition friend.date_of_birth equals |1984-01-01|
  definition friend.gross_income equals $2,000
  assertion not c.r.dep.qualifying_child
  assertion c.r.dep.qualifying_relative
  assertion c.r.hoh_other_relative_path
  assertion c.r.hoh_qualifying_person
  # Known-bad: under half the year
  assertion short.r.dep.qualifying_relative
  assertion not short.r.hoh_qualifying_person
  # Known-bad: a friend is a qualifying relative but not a qualifying person
  assertion friend.r.dep.qualifying_relative
  assertion friend.r.dep.eligible_dependent
  assertion not friend.r.hoh_qualifying_person
```

### Married but considered unmarried: only a child qualifies

IRC 2(c), 7703(b)(1) ("a child (within the meaning of section 152(f)(1))");
Pub. 501 p 9, Considered Unmarried, test 4 ("your child, stepchild, or foster
child"). The filer is married (`eligible_for_mfj`) and lived apart from the
spouse for the last six months. The son and a foster daughter (both
qualifying children and dependents) qualify; the brother of the previous test
does not, although he would for an unmarried filer.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMarriedConsideredUnmarried:
  son scope Case
  foster scope Case
  brother scope Case

scope TestMarriedConsideredUnmarried:
  definition son.eligible_for_mfj equals true
  definition foster.eligible_for_mfj equals true
  definition foster.relationship equals Q.Relationship.FosterChild
  definition brother.eligible_for_mfj equals true
  definition brother.relationship equals Q.Relationship.Sibling
  definition brother.date_of_birth equals |1990-01-01|
  definition brother.residency equals Q.ResidencyDuration.SixToElevenMonths
  definition brother.gross_income equals $2,000
  assertion son.r.considered_unmarried_child
  assertion son.r.hoh_qualifying_person
  assertion foster.r.married_hoh_relationship_test
  assertion foster.r.hoh_qualifying_person
  # Known-bad: the brother passes the third branch but is not a child
  assertion not brother.r.married_hoh_relationship_test
  assertion brother.r.hoh_other_relative_path
  assertion not brother.r.hoh_qualifying_person
```

### QSS: all-year residence, foster child excluded

IRC 2(a)(1)(B) ("for the taxable year the principal place of abode"; "a son,
stepson, daughter, or stepdaughter"); Pub. 501 p 10, tests 3 ("a child or
stepchild (not a foster child)") and 4 ("This child lived in your home all
year"). The filer could qualify for QSS. The son who lived there all year
qualifies; the same son who lived there eight months does not (but is still a
HoH qualifying person); a foster daughter who lived there all year does not
(but is a HoH qualifying person); a stepdaughter does.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestQss:
  son scope Case
  part_year scope Case
  foster scope Case
  step scope Case

scope TestQss:
  definition son.filer_could_qualify_for_qss equals true
  definition part_year.filer_could_qualify_for_qss equals true
  definition part_year.residency equals Q.ResidencyDuration.SixToElevenMonths
  definition foster.filer_could_qualify_for_qss equals true
  definition foster.relationship equals Q.Relationship.FosterChild
  definition step.filer_could_qualify_for_qss equals true
  definition step.relationship equals Q.Relationship.StepChild
  assertion son.r.qss_person_residency_test
  assertion son.r.qss_qualifying_person
  assertion son.r.person_qualifies_tp_for_qss
  # Known-bad: eight months
  assertion not part_year.r.qss_person_residency_test
  assertion not part_year.r.qss_qualifying_person
  assertion part_year.r.hoh_qualifying_person
  # Known-bad: foster child
  assertion not foster.r.qss_qualifying_person
  assertion foster.r.hoh_qualifying_person
  assertion step.r.qss_qualifying_person
```

### QSS disregards the gross income test; HoH does not

IRC 2(a)(1)(B)(i) ("determined without regard to subsections (b)(1), (b)(2),
and (d)(1)(B)"); Pub. 501 p 10, test 3a ("The child had gross income of
$5,050 or more"). A 25-year-old daughter with $6,000 of gross income, all year
at home, supported over half by the filer: a QSS qualifying person, but not a
HoH qualifying person (Pub. 501 p 9, Example 2: not a qualifying child by age,
not a qualifying relative by gross income).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestQssGrossIncomeDisregarded:
  c scope Case

scope TestQssGrossIncomeDisregarded:
  definition c.date_of_birth equals |1999-03-01|
  definition c.gross_income equals $6,000
  definition c.filer_could_qualify_for_qss equals true
  assertion not c.r.dep.qualifying_child
  assertion not c.r.dep.qualifying_relative
  assertion c.r.qss_qualifying_person
  assertion not c.r.hoh_qualifying_person
```

### No TIN: excluded

A brother with no SSN, ITIN or ATIN cannot be claimed (IRC 151(e)), so he is
not a HoH qualifying person through the other-relative path. An unmarried son
with no TIN is still a qualifying child and a qualifying person (IRC
2(b)(1)(A)(i) asks for no deduction), but DF does not support a HoH return
whose qualifying person has no TIN (`/knockoutHohQpHasNoTin`): the household
test below knocks it out unless another qualifying person has a TIN.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestNoTinPerson:
  brother scope Case
  son scope Case

scope TestNoTinPerson:
  definition brother.relationship equals Q.Relationship.Sibling
  definition brother.date_of_birth equals |1990-01-01|
  definition brother.residency equals Q.ResidencyDuration.SixToElevenMonths
  definition brother.gross_income equals $2,000
  definition brother.tin_type equals R.TinType.NoTin
  definition son.tin_type equals R.TinType.NoTin
  assertion brother.r.dep.qualifying_relative
  assertion not brother.r.dep.eligible_dependent
  assertion not brother.r.hoh_qualifying_person
  assertion son.r.hoh_qualifying_person
  assertion not son.r.hoh_qp_has_tin
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestNoTinHousehold:
  son scope Case
  daughter scope Case
  internal only_no_tin content H.HohQssPersons
  internal with_tin content H.HohQssPersons
  internal single content H.HohQssPersons

scope TestNoTinHousehold:
  definition son.tin_type equals R.TinType.NoTin
  definition daughter.date_of_birth equals |2018-09-09|
  definition only_no_tin equals
    output of H.HohQssPersons with {
      -- members: [son.member]
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true
      -- treat_as_mfj: false
      -- eligible_for_mfj: false
      -- filer_could_qualify_for_hoh: true
      -- filer_could_qualify_for_qss: false
      -- filing_status: Types.FilingStatus.HeadOfHousehold }
  definition with_tin equals
    output of H.HohQssPersons with {
      -- members: [son.member; daughter.member]
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true
      -- treat_as_mfj: false
      -- eligible_for_mfj: false
      -- filer_could_qualify_for_hoh: true
      -- filer_could_qualify_for_qss: false
      -- filing_status: Types.FilingStatus.HeadOfHousehold }
  definition single equals
    output of H.HohQssPersons with {
      -- members: [son.member]
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true
      -- treat_as_mfj: false
      -- eligible_for_mfj: false
      -- filer_could_qualify_for_hoh: true
      -- filer_could_qualify_for_qss: false
      -- filing_status: Types.FilingStatus.Single }
  assertion only_no_tin.hoh_qualifying_people_count = 1
  assertion only_no_tin.hoh_qualifying_people_with_tin_count = 0
  assertion only_no_tin.ko_knockout_hoh_qp_has_no_tin
  assertion only_no_tin.unsupported
  # Known-bad: another qualifying person with a TIN is chosen, no knockout
  assertion with_tin.hoh_qualifying_people_count = 2
  assertion with_tin.hoh_qualifying_people_with_tin_count = 1
  assertion with_tin.has_hoh_qualifying_child
  assertion not with_tin.has_hoh_qualifying_parent
  assertion not with_tin.ko_knockout_hoh_qp_has_no_tin
  # Known-bad: not filing as head of household, no knockout
  assertion not single.ko_knockout_hoh_qp_has_no_tin
  assertion not single.unsupported
```

## Benefit split and the tie-breakers

### The custodial parent who released the claim keeps HoH, not QSS

Pub. 501 p 10, Table 4 footnote 1: "If you are the custodial parent and those
rules apply, the child is generally your qualifying child for head of
household filing status even though the child isn't a qualifying child you
can claim as a dependent." QSS needs a child "with respect to whom the
taxpayer is entitled to a deduction" (IRC 2(a)(1)(B)(ii)). The same holds
for a married filer living apart: IRC 7703(b)(1), "or would be so entitled
but for section 152(e)".

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestCustodialRelease:
  c scope Case
  married scope Case

scope TestCustodialRelease:
  definition c.custodial_release equals true
  definition c.filer_could_qualify_for_qss equals true
  definition married.custodial_release equals true
  definition married.eligible_for_mfj equals true
  assertion c.r.dep.split.tp_can_claim_split_benefits_hoh_eitc_cdcc
  assertion not c.r.dep.eligible_dependent
  assertion c.r.hoh_qualifying_person
  # Known-bad: QSS
  assertion not c.r.qss_qualifying_person
  assertion married.r.considered_unmarried_child
  assertion married.r.hoh_qualifying_person
```

### A grandparent who loses the child to the parent under the tie-breaker

Pub. 501 p 18, Example 2: "Your parent can't claim Kody as a qualifying child
for any purpose because your parent's AGI isn't higher than yours." The
grandson lives with the filer all year and is the filer's qualifying child
under 152(c), but is `disqualified_due_to_parental_custody`.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestGrandparentDisqualified:
  c scope Case
  plain scope Case

scope TestGrandparentDisqualified:
  definition c.relationship equals Q.Relationship.GrandChildOrOtherDescendantOfChild
  definition c.date_of_birth equals |2019-03-01|
  definition c.minimum_filer_date_of_birth equals |1960-06-15|
  definition c.grandparent_lower_agi equals true
  definition plain.relationship equals Q.Relationship.GrandChildOrOtherDescendantOfChild
  definition plain.date_of_birth equals |2019-03-01|
  definition plain.minimum_filer_date_of_birth equals |1960-06-15|
  assertion c.r.dep.split.disqualified_due_to_parental_custody
  assertion c.r.hoh_qualifying_child_path
  assertion not c.r.hoh_qualifying_person
  # Known-bad: without the split the grandson qualifies the grandparent
  assertion plain.r.hoh_qualifying_person
```

### The qualifying child of another taxpayer must be claimed

DF's encoding of the tie-breakers of IRC 152(c)(4) (Q6): a child who is also
the qualifying child of another taxpayer counts only if the filer claims the
child.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestQualifyingChildOfAnother:
  claimed scope Case
  unclaimed scope Case

scope TestQualifyingChildOfAnother:
  definition claimed.could_be_qc_of_another equals true
  definition claimed.potential_claimer_must_file equals true
  definition unclaimed.could_be_qc_of_another equals true
  definition unclaimed.potential_claimer_must_file equals true
  definition unclaimed.tp_claims equals false
  assertion claimed.r.dep.is_qualifying_child_of_another
  assertion claimed.r.hoh_qualifying_person
  assertion unclaimed.r.dep.is_qualifying_child_of_another
  assertion not unclaimed.r.hoh_qualifying_person
```

## Divergences from Direct File (CONVENTIONS section 8)

### DF-BUG(19-a): a child the married filer cannot claim does not make them unmarried

IRC 7703(b)(1); Pub. 501 p 9, Considered Unmarried, test 5. A married filer
living apart whose only child has no TIN (151(e)) cannot claim the child, so
is not considered unmarried. DF says the child is a HoH qualifying person.
The same son for an unmarried filer still qualifies (2(b)(1)(A)(i)).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestDfBug19aMarriedChildNoTin:
  married scope Case
  unmarried scope Case

scope TestDfBug19aMarriedChildNoTin:
  definition married.eligible_for_mfj equals true
  definition married.tin_type equals R.TinType.NoTin
  definition unmarried.tin_type equals R.TinType.NoTin
  assertion married.r.married_hoh_relationship_test
  assertion not married.r.considered_unmarried_child
  assertion married.r.hoh_qualifying_child_path
  assertion not married.r.hoh_qualifying_person
  assertion unmarried.r.hoh_qualifying_person
```

### DF-BUG(19-b): a dependent the filer chose not to claim still qualifies

IRC 2(b)(1), 2(a)(1)(B); Pub. 501 p 9, How to file ("If the child who
qualifies you for this filing status isn't claimed as your dependent ...,
enter the child's name"). DF requires `isClaimedIfClaimable`.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestDfBug19bUnclaimed:
  c scope Case

scope TestDfBug19bUnclaimed:
  definition c.tp_claims equals false
  definition c.filer_could_qualify_for_qss equals true
  assertion c.r.dep.eligible_dependent
  assertion not c.r.dep.is_claimed_if_claimable
  assertion c.r.hoh_qualifying_person
  assertion c.r.qss_qualifying_person
```

### DF-BUG(19-c): the married-child exclusion is only for 152(b)(2) and (b)(3)

IRC 2(b)(1)(A)(i)(I)-(II). A married 17-year-old son who did not file a joint
return and has no TIN: a qualifying person here, not in DF. Known-bad outputs
rejected: the same married son who filed a joint return (not a qualifying
child, 152(c)(1)(E)), and a married son who is not a citizen or resident
(152(b)(3)).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestDfBug19cMarriedChild:
  no_tin scope Case
  joint scope Case
  foreign scope Case

scope TestDfBug19cMarriedChild:
  definition no_tin.date_of_birth equals |2007-02-01|
  definition no_tin.married equals true
  definition no_tin.tin_type equals R.TinType.NoTin
  definition joint.date_of_birth equals |2007-02-01|
  definition joint.married equals true
  definition joint.writable_joint_return equals true
  definition foreign.date_of_birth equals |2007-02-01|
  definition foreign.married equals true
  definition foreign.citizen equals false
  assertion no_tin.r.dep.qualifying_child
  assertion not no_tin.r.dep.eligible_dependent_minus_filer_information
  assertion no_tin.r.married_child_not_excluded
  assertion no_tin.r.hoh_qualifying_person
  # Known-bad: joint return
  assertion not joint.r.dep.qualifying_child
  assertion not joint.r.hoh_qualifying_person
  # Known-bad: 152(b)(3)
  assertion not foreign.r.married_child_not_excluded
  assertion not foreign.r.hoh_qualifying_person
```

### DF-BUG(19-d): a qualifying relative on the filer's side of a split

IRC 2(b)(1)(A)(ii). A married 16-year-old son who filed a joint return (so
not a qualifying child) and whose custody split lets the filer keep HoH,
EITC and CDCC benefits: he is the filer's qualifying relative but not a
dependent the filer may claim, so not a qualifying person. DF says he is.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestDfBug19dSplitRelative:
  c scope Case

scope TestDfBug19dSplitRelative:
  definition c.date_of_birth equals |2008-02-01|
  definition c.married equals true
  definition c.writable_joint_return equals true
  definition c.gross_income equals $1,000
  definition c.custodial_release equals true
  assertion not c.r.dep.qualifying_child
  assertion c.r.dep.qualifying_relative
  assertion c.r.dep.split.tp_can_claim_split_benefits_hoh_eitc_cdcc
  assertion not c.r.dep.eligible_dependent
  assertion not c.r.hoh_other_relative_path
  assertion not c.r.hoh_qualifying_person
```

## The household

A son, the filer's mother living apart, and a lodger: two HoH qualifying
persons (one of them a parent), one QSS qualifying person.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestHousehold:
  son scope Case
  mother scope Case
  lodger scope Case
  internal h content H.HohQssPersons

scope TestHousehold:
  definition mother.relationship equals Q.Relationship.Parent
  definition mother.date_of_birth equals |1950-04-02|
  definition mother.residency equals Q.ResidencyDuration.LessThanSixMonths
  definition mother.gross_income equals $3,000
  definition mother.parent_upkeep equals true
  definition lodger.relationship equals Q.Relationship.NoneOfTheAbove
  definition lodger.date_of_birth equals |1984-01-01|
  definition lodger.gross_income equals $2,000
  definition h equals
    output of H.HohQssPersons with {
      -- members: [son.member; mother.member; lodger.member]
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true
      -- treat_as_mfj: false
      -- eligible_for_mfj: false
      -- filer_could_qualify_for_hoh: true
      -- filer_could_qualify_for_qss: true
      -- filing_status: Types.FilingStatus.QualifyingSurvivingSpouse }
  assertion number of h.results = 3
  assertion h.hoh_qualifying_people_count = 2
  assertion h.qss_qualifying_people_count = 1
  assertion h.has_hoh_qualifying_child
  assertion h.has_hoh_qualifying_parent
  assertion not h.unsupported
```
